This was the first time I'd done some heavy alchemizing, and it shows
in the HP field. Decided to level up as much as I could, if only for
the challenge (and the original notion to go extinctionist - I figured
I needed levels to get create monster to create monsters of high
difficulty). Burdened on Astral = bad, but I needed to drag that
blessed (BoH to the altar. However, a knight with the Magic Mirror
of Merlin _and_ the foresight to drop the "AoY before casting magic
missile _is_ well-night unstoppable. O yeah, that was another reason
to level up: 23d6 for MM is lots of damage.



What happened: memory fails, and I didn't take notes, and the game
ended late late at night, so things are hazy. There was some early 
toying with a magic whistle and a pet - which was then fatal for
shopkeepers. Found a huge armor store on DL3, most useful. Co-aligned
minetown. Another altar on DL9. A cross-aligned temple on DL16. Got all of 
Ludios, Rogue, Bigroom. Refunds of 70k were arranged. Spent much time
doing inventory management at stashes on DL9 and DL16. Finally got
sick of it. Left behind gobs and gobs of scrolls and potions and
whatnot.

There is no hearse on this machine, but a few collegues play on it,
so there are in fact interesting bones files. I think I got three,
from Joe, who is trying to ascend in alphabetical order and is 
currently struggling with B. One had Mojo, another had fallen down
the stairs with a footrice. So his statue made a nice rockery,
and his gear was mine (on DL23).

I tried riding dragons for a while, but hand-to-hand was antsy,
especially when Puff was turned to stone by a 'trice underneath me.
Glad that doesn't stun you for a few turns. Later a ki-rin was my
steed, which lasted a long time except: eventually I dismounted,
the saddle cursed, and I didn't know what to do. Thought that his
tameness was too low, left him behind for many turns till peaceful,
tried charm monster many times. No dice. Tried to cancel the peaceful
ki-rin, oops. Fought my way out of that, and a lucky charm monster
brought him back into the fold. Along with many others, who were abandoned
here and there. Not very lawful, is it.

Finally turned to spoilers, and found that that wand of opening was
actually useful. Used it several times, like also when I got stuck
in the saddle.

Gehennom something of a bore, did wait for some extra lawful demon
lords (princes?), didn't wait for Yeeno or the big D. Probably should have.

The dungeon was very very deep, Medusa was DL26, I think. And the
VS at DL52. Did the ol' light at the stairs trick, dug out the mazes,
stuck around the altar for long long time using up /CM, ?CM and +CM,
finally tried sacrificing that white unicorn mentioned earlier,
decided to just make an end to it. Did pauze long enough to eat
some +1 rings of increase damage, but it seems they didn't add _much_
to me (do you gain randomly up to the ring enchantment, or what?).

Final run uneventful, herded several pets into the Astral plane, but
not many survived. Right, Famine, a bit edgy - I'd brought a glaive
so I could hit the Riders from afar, but that would only work with no
pets and lots of ants, which just didn't show up. Wrong altar. Middle,
Pestilence, no problem. Used more magic missile now.

And that was that. Healers up next. Must decide what kind of conduct
will be appropriate there - conduct I'll forget about, of course.



